{# ============================================================================
   THE DEPARTMENT THESIS, AS A CONTROL.

   A lens RE-ORDERS AND PRE-SELECTS; it never fences. Switching it changes ONE
   query parameter and no permission, and the "Every category" chip is always
   present, so nothing is ever out of reach. The note beside it says so in words,
   because a control whose limits are only in the code is a control people will
   eventually assume the worst about.

   → GET /areas/{uuid}/modules/incidents?lens=protection|ecology|all
   ========================================================================== #}
{% set lenses = {} %}
{% for category in dashboard.categories %}
    {% for lead in category.leads %}
        {% set lenses = lenses|merge({(lead|lower|split(' ')|first): lead}) %}
    {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

<div class="i-lensbar">
    <span class="lbl">Lens</span>
    {% for key, label in lenses %}
        <a class="i-lens{{ filter.lens == key ? ' on' }}" href="{{ path('incident_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}|merge(filter.toQuery|merge({lens: key}))) }}" data-lens="{{ key }}">{{ label }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
    <a class="i-lens{{ filter.lens == 'all' ? ' on' }}" href="{{ path('incident_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}|merge(filter.toQuery|merge({lens: 'all'}))) }}" data-lens="all">Every category</a>
</div>
<div class="i-lensnote">{{ ux_icon('lucide:info') }}<div><b>A lens, not a fence.</b> A department attaching this module changes what its team
    sees <b>first</b> — never what data exists or who may read it. One click on <b>Every category</b> shows the whole
    register to anybody, and no department can hide a row from another.</div></div>
